Local netboot detection fix for usb-signaller v0.4.2.
Upstream: https://codeberg.org/DylanVanAssche/usb-signaller/src/tag/v0.4.2

A kernel with built-in NBD creates idle /dev/nbd0..15 at boot, so the
existence of /dev/nbd0 made every boot look like netboot: the service
refused to change the read-only mode and exited, and systemd restarted it
forever. Treat netboot as active only while nbd0 is connected; the kernel
creates /sys/block/nbd0/pid only then.

--- a/src/udc.rs
+++ b/src/udc.rs
@@ -67,6 +67,6 @@
 impl UDC {
     fn detect_netboot_mode() -> bool {
-        /* Netboot hook creates /dev/nbd0 and starts a NBD client */
-        return PathBuf::from("/dev/nbd0").exists();
+        /* Netboot hook connects /dev/nbd0 through an NBD client */
+        return PathBuf::from("/sys/block/nbd0/pid").exists();
     }
 
